#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:244
msgid ""
"Last, make a folder for it under ~/Cloud, where the cloud folders are "
"gathered, and mount it there. Run these in a terminal:"
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:248
msgid ""
"--vfs-cache-mode full keeps a copy of what is used on this computer, and --"
"dir-cache-time remembers the lists of files for an hour: without them, Files "
"fetches every file to show the folder, which can take minutes. --volname "
"gives it the name the file manager shows, and --umask 077 shows what is "
"there as yours alone, as it is: other accounts cannot reach a mount like "
"this. --daemon lets it run in the background until you log out. To mount it "
"each time you log in, rclone's own documentation shows how."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:256
msgid ""
"Use the encrypted setup, as above, for everything you put there: what goes "
"through the other one is not encrypted."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:302
msgid ""
"A file of that name is there already, and it is not this one, so it was left "
"as it is."
msgstr ""

#: src/plugins/cloud/gaudit-cloud.c:304
